cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "breakpointdrift: separate breakpoint revisions and reporting-rule changes from change under fixed criteria in antimicrobial resistance trends"
abstract: "R package that reinterprets raw MICs and zone diameters under CLSI and EUCAST editions, splits each organism and drug's change in percent resistant into a criteria component and a fixed-criteria component, tests both by bootstrap, and estimates MIC shifts with an interval-censored model."
authors:
  - given-names: "M."
    family-names: Ualiyev
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9389-0158"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/FerrumSL/breakpoint-drift"
keywords: [antimicrobial resistance, breakpoints, antibiogram, surveillance, R]
